WEBVTT

00:04:58.621 --> 00:05:01.871
Each of us had a before and an after.

00:05:02.746 --> 00:05:05.204
I'd been working through my lot after all.

00:05:06.163 --> 00:05:08.913
Still, Abed was far from my mind,

00:05:08.954 --> 00:05:12.621
when last year, I returned to Israel
to write of the crash,

00:05:12.621 --> 00:05:15.454
and the book I then wrote, "Half-Life,"

00:05:15.454 --> 00:05:18.288
was nearly complete when I recognized

00:05:18.288 --> 00:05:20.204
that I still wanted to meet Abed.

00:05:20.746 --> 00:05:23.454
And finally, I understood why:

00:05:23.496 --> 00:05:26.954
to hear this man say two words:

00:05:26.954 --> 00:05:28.204
"I'm sorry."

00:05:29.079 --> 00:05:31.038
People apologize for less.